'' T43, RUN: a lambda held in a 'var' is called inside a generic member, as fbc-modern
'' allows -- instantiated at long, and in a generic nothing instantiates. In the
'' TEMPLATE's own body the lambda over T is not hoisted yet, so 'f' typed as a pointer to
'' its result and 'f( a, b )' was TKO0772; the call is judged in the instance, where 'f'
'' is a procedure pointer. The same lambda in a plain sub was always fine. Output
'' identical to fbc-modern's. See symbols/tmpllocal.bas.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/lambda-var-in-generic.bas -o tests/codegen/lambdavaringeneric.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/codegen/lambdavaringeneric.exe
'' RUN: tests/codegen/lambdavaringeneric.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: true
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: true
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: end
